IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc16-preservation.l4 -- sections 487.011 to 487.0131 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (Part XV): the definitions for sections 487.011 to 487.0199,
-- the preservation demand, the preservation order, and the keep-account-open-or-active order.
-- Part agent ccc16. Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Imports the keel's core only.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Conventions: as in ccc16-open-court.l4. Periods are dates: `Date day month year`; "N days after the day on which it is made" is the made day PLUS N days, the order being in effect on the days before that day
-- (a boundary reading, fork F-EXP in NOTES.md). Where the text says "reasonable grounds to suspect" or "to believe" the person asks whether the justice or judge is satisfied, not whether the grounds exist.
-- "A person who is under investigation for the offence ... may not be made subject to an order" is a bar for the person asking (JUST TRUE where they are under investigation).
-- Seams: `s 342.1(2) computer data and computer system` (MAYBE BOOLEAN, ccc12), `s 2 public officer` (MAYBE BOOLEAN).

§ `Section 487.011 -- Definitions`

-- 487.011 The following definitions apply in this section and in sections 487.012 to 487.0199.
-- Section numbers are decimals: 487.012 to 487.0199 takes in 487.0131, 487.0194 and 487.0199 but not 487.02.
-- src:9059 | 487.011 The following definitions apply in this section and in sections 487.012 to 487.0199.
@ref s 487.011 (the scope: this section and sections 487.012 to 487.0199) (src:9059)
GIVEN `the section the term is used in` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.011 the definitions apply in the section` MEANS
    IF    `the section the term is used in` EQUALS 487.011
       OR (`the section the term is used in` AT LEAST 487.012 AND `the section the term is used in` AT MOST 487.0199)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The following definitions apply in this section and in sections 487.012 to 487.0199."

-- computer data has the same meaning as in subsection 342.1(2): the meaning is in another part, so the answer is an input.
-- src:9060 | computer data has the same meaning as in subsection 342.1(2). (données informatiques)
@ref s 487.011 "computer data" (src:9060)
GIVEN `s 342.1(2) computer data and computer system: the thing is computer data` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.011 computer data` MEANS
    `s 342.1(2) computer data and computer system: the thing is computer data`   -- passes JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING through; NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) when the answer of subsection 342.1(2) is not given

-- src:9061 | data means representations, including signs, signals or symbols, that are capable of being understood by an individual or processed by a computer system or other device. (données)
@ref s 487.011 "data" (src:9061)
GIVEN `the thing is a representation, including signs, signals or symbols` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the representation is capable of being understood by an individual or processed by a computer system or other device` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.011 data` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a representation, including signs, signals or symbols` AND `the representation is capable of being understood by an individual or processed by a computer system or other device`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "data means representations, including signs, signals or symbols, that are capable of being understood by an individual or processed by a computer system or other device"

-- src:9062 | document means a medium on which data is registered or marked. (document)
@ref s 487.011 "document" (src:9062)
GIVEN `the thing is a medium` IS A BOOLEAN
      `data is registered or marked on the medium` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.011 document` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a medium` AND `data is registered or marked on the medium`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "document means a medium on which data is registered or marked"

DECLARE `s 487.011 the court the judge sits in` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.011 a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction`
    `s 487.011 a judge of the Court of Quebec`
    `s 487.011 a judge of another court`

-- src:9063 | judge means a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge of the Court of Quebec. (juge)
@ref s 487.011 "judge" (src:9063)
GIVEN court IS A `s 487.011 the court the judge sits in`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.011 judge` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `s 487.011 a judge of another court` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "judge means a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge of the Court of Quebec"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- public officer means a public officer who is appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this Act or any other Act of Parliament.
-- src:9064 | public officer means a public officer who is appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this Act or any other Act of Parliament. (fonctionnaire public)
@ref s 487.011 "public officer" (src:9064)
GIVEN `s 2 public officer: the person is a public officer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's duties include the enforcement of this Act or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.011 public officer` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2 public officer: the person is a public officer`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a public officer at all is for the definition in section 2
    WHEN JUST isOfficer THEN
        IF isOfficer AND `the person is appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law` AND `the person's duties include the enforcement of this Act or any other Act of Parliament`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "public officer means a public officer who is appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this Act or any other Act of Parliament"

-- src:9065 | tracking data means data that relates to the location of a transaction, individual or thing. (données de localisation)
@ref s 487.011 "tracking data" (src:9065)
GIVEN `s 487.011 data: the thing is data` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the data relates to the location of a transaction, individual or thing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.011 tracking data` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 487.011 data: the thing is data`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the thing is data is the answer of the definition of data, not given
    WHEN JUST isData THEN
        IF isData AND `the data relates to the location of a transaction, individual or thing`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "tracking data means data that relates to the location of a transaction, individual or thing"

-- transmission data means data that (a) relates to the telecommunication functions of dialling, routing, addressing or signalling; (b) is transmitted to identify, activate or configure a device, ... in order to establish or maintain access
-- to a telecommunication service for the purpose of enabling a communication, or is generated during the creation, transmission or reception of a communication and identifies or purports to identify the type, direction, date, time, duration, size, origin,
-- destination or termination of the communication; and (c) does not reveal the substance, meaning or purpose of the communication.
-- src:9066 | transmission data means data that
-- src:9067 | (a) relates to the telecommunication functions of dialling, routing, addressing or signalling;
-- src:9068 | (b) is transmitted to identify, activate or configure a device, including a computer program as defined in subsection 342.1(2), in order to establish or maintain access to a telecommunication service for the purpose of enabling a communication, or is generated during the creation, transmission or reception of a communication and identifies or purports to identify the type, direction, date, time, duration, size, origin, destination or termination of the communication; and
-- src:9069 | (c) does not reveal the substance, meaning or purpose of the communication. (données de transmission)
@ref s 487.011 "transmission data" (a), (b), (c) (src:9066-9069)
GIVEN `s 487.011 data: the thing is data` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the data relates to the telecommunication functions of dialling, routing, addressing or signalling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data is transmitted to identify, activate or configure a device, including a computer program as defined in subsection 342.1(2), in order to establish or maintain access to a telecommunication service for the purpose of enabling a communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data is generated during the creation, transmission or reception of a communication and identifies or purports to identify the type, direction, date, time, duration, size, origin, destination or termination of the communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data does not reveal the substance, meaning or purpose of the communication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.011 transmission data` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 487.011 data: the thing is data`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the thing is data is the answer of the definition of data, not given
    WHEN JUST isData THEN
        IF isData
           AND `the data relates to the telecommunication functions of dialling, routing, addressing or signalling`
           AND (`the data is transmitted to identify, activate or configure a device, including a computer program as defined in subsection 342.1(2), in order to establish or maintain access to a telecommunication service for the purpose of enabling a communication` OR `the data is generated during the creation, transmission or reception of a communication and identifies or purports to identify the type, direction, date, time, duration, size, origin, destination or termination of the communication`)
           AND `the data does not reveal the substance, meaning or purpose of the communication`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "transmission data means data that"

§ `Section 487.012 -- Preservation demand`

-- 487.012(1) A peace officer or public officer may make a demand to a person in Form 5.001 requiring them to preserve computer data that is in their possession or control when the demand is made.
-- src:9070 | Preservation demand
-- src:9071 | 487.012 (1) A peace officer or public officer may make a demand to a person in Form 5.001 requiring them to preserve computer data that is in their possession or control when the demand is made.
@ref s 487.012(1) (src:9070-9071)
GIVEN `the person making the demand is a peace officer or public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the demand is in Form 5.001` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the computer data is in the person's possession or control when the demand is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.012(1) the peace officer or public officer may make a demand to preserve computer data` MEANS
    IF `the person making the demand is a peace officer or public officer` AND `the demand is in Form 5.001` AND `the computer data is in the person's possession or control when the demand is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may make a demand to a person in Form 5.001 requiring them to preserve computer data that is in their possession or control when the demand is made"

-- 487.012(2) The peace officer or public officer may make the demand only if they have reasonable grounds to suspect that (a) an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament or has been committed under a law of a foreign state;
-- (b) in the case of an offence committed under a law of a foreign state, an investigation is being conducted by a person or authority with responsibility in that state for the investigation of such offences; and (c) the computer data is in the person's
-- possession or control and will assist in the investigation of the offence.
-- src:9072 | Conditions for making demand
-- src:9073 | (2) The peace officer or public officer may make the demand only if they have reasonable grounds to suspect that
-- src:9074 | (a) an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament or has been committed under a law of a foreign state;
-- src:9075 | (b) in the case of an offence committed under a law of a foreign state, an investigation is being conducted by a person or authority with responsibility in that state for the investigation of such offences; and
-- src:9076 | (c) the computer data is in the person’s possession or control and will assist in the investigation of the offence.
@ref s 487.012(2)(a), (b), (c) (src:9072-9076)
GIVEN `the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that an offence has been committed under a law of a foreign state` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an investigation is being conducted by a person or authority with responsibility in that state for the investigation of such offences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that the computer data is in the person's possession or control and will assist in the investigation of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.012(2) the peace officer or public officer may make the demand` MEANS
    IF    (`the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament` OR `the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that an offence has been committed under a law of a foreign state`)
      AND ((NOT `the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that an offence has been committed under a law of a foreign state`) OR `an investigation is being conducted by a person or authority with responsibility in that state for the investigation of such offences`)
      AND `the officer has reasonable grounds to suspect that the computer data is in the person's possession or control and will assist in the investigation of the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The peace officer or public officer may make the demand only if they have reasonable grounds to suspect that"

-- 487.012(3) A demand may not be made to a person who is under investigation for the offence referred to in paragraph (2)(a). The answer is the bar.
-- src:9077 | Limitation
-- src:9078 | (3) A demand may not be made to a person who is under investigation for the offence referred to in paragraph (2)(a).
@ref s 487.012(3) (src:9077-9078)
GIVEN `the person is under investigation for the offence referred to in paragraph (2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.012(3) the demand is barred against the person under investigation for the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person is under investigation for the offence referred to in paragraph (2)(a)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A demand may not be made to a person who is under investigation for the offence referred to in paragraph (2)(a)"

-- 487.012(4) A peace officer or public officer may revoke the demand by notice given to the person at any time. Unless the demand is revoked earlier, the demand expires (a) in the case of an offence that has been or will be committed under this or any
-- other Act of Parliament, 21 days after the day on which it is made; and (b) in the case of an offence committed under a law of a foreign state, 90 days after the day on which it is made.
-- src:9079 | Expiry and revocation of demand
-- src:9080 | (4) A peace officer or public officer may revoke the demand by notice given to the person at any time. Unless the demand is revoked earlier, the demand expires
-- src:9081 | (a) in the case of an offence that has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament, 21 days after the day on which it is made; and
-- src:9082 | (b) in the case of an offence committed under a law of a foreign state, 90 days after the day on which it is made.
@ref s 487.012(4) (revocation) (src:9079-9082)
GIVEN `the revocation is by notice given to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.012(4) the peace officer or public officer may revoke the demand` MEANS
    IF `the revocation is by notice given to the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may revoke the demand by notice given to the person at any time"

DECLARE `s 487.012(4) the kind of offence the demand concerns` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.012(4)(a) an offence that has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament`
    `s 487.012(4)(b) an offence committed under a law of a foreign state`

-- src:9079 | Expiry and revocation of demand
-- src:9080 | (4) A peace officer or public officer may revoke the demand by notice given to the person at any time. Unless the demand is revoked earlier, the demand expires
-- src:9081 | (a) in the case of an offence that has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament, 21 days after the day on which it is made; and
-- src:9082 | (b) in the case of an offence committed under a law of a foreign state, 90 days after the day on which it is made.
@ref s 487.012(4) (expiry) (src:9079-9082)
GIVEN `the day the demand is made` IS A DATE
      kind IS A `s 487.012(4) the kind of offence the demand concerns`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 487.012(4) the demand expires on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 487.012(4)(a) an offence that has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament` THEN `the day the demand is made` PLUS 21
    WHEN `s 487.012(4)(b) an offence committed under a law of a foreign state` THEN `the day the demand is made` PLUS 90

@ref s 487.012(4) (in effect) (src:9079-9082)
GIVEN `the day the demand is made` IS A DATE
      kind IS A `s 487.012(4) the kind of offence the demand concerns`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the day the demand was revoked, if it was revoked earlier` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.012(4) the demand is in effect on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the demand was revoked, if it was revoked earlier`
    WHEN JUST revoked THEN
        IF `the day in question` AT LEAST revoked
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless the demand is revoked earlier"
        ELSE IF `the day in question` LESS THAN `s 487.012(4) the demand expires on the day` `the day the demand is made` kind THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the demand expires"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the day in question` LESS THAN `s 487.012(4) the demand expires on the day` `the day the demand is made` kind
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the demand expires"

-- 487.012(5) The peace officer or public officer who makes the demand may impose any conditions in the demand that they consider appropriate -- including conditions prohibiting the disclosure of its existence or some or all of its contents -- and may revoke a condition at any time by notice given to the person.
-- src:9083 | Conditions in demand
-- src:9084 | (5) The peace officer or public officer who makes the demand may impose any conditions in the demand that they consider appropriate — including conditions prohibiting the disclosure of its existence or some or all of its contents — and may revoke a condition at any time by notice given to the person.
@ref s 487.012(5) (src:9083-9084)
GIVEN `the condition is one that the officer considers appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.012(5) the officer who makes the demand may impose the condition in the demand` MEANS
    IF `the condition is one that the officer considers appropriate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any conditions in the demand that they consider appropriate"

-- src:9083 | Conditions in demand
-- src:9084 | (5) The peace officer or public officer who makes the demand may impose any conditions in the demand that they consider appropriate — including conditions prohibiting the disclosure of its existence or some or all of its contents — and may revoke a condition at any time by notice given to the person.
@ref s 487.012(5) (revoking a condition) (src:9083-9084)
GIVEN `the condition is revoked by notice given to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.012(5) the officer may revoke the condition at any time` MEANS
    IF `the condition is revoked by notice given to the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may revoke a condition at any time by notice given to the person"

-- 487.012(6) A peace officer or public officer may not make another demand requiring the person to preserve the same computer data in connection with the investigation. The answer is the bar.
-- src:9085 | No further demand
-- src:9086 | (6) A peace officer or public officer may not make another demand requiring the person to preserve the same computer data in connection with the investigation.
@ref s 487.012(6) (src:9085-9086)
GIVEN `a demand has already been made to the person to preserve the same computer data in connection with the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.012(6) another demand to preserve the same computer data in connection with the investigation is barred` MEANS
    IF `a demand has already been made to the person to preserve the same computer data in connection with the investigation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may not make another demand requiring the person to preserve the same computer data in connection with the investigation"

§ `Section 487.013 -- Preservation order -- computer data`

-- 487.013(1) On ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer, a justice or judge may order a person to preserve computer data that is in their possession or control when they receive the order.
-- src:9087 | Preservation order — computer data
-- src:9088 | 487.013 (1) On ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer, a justice or judge may order a person to preserve computer data that is in their possession or control when they receive the order.
@ref s 487.013(1) (src:9087-9088)
GIVEN `the application is made ex parte by a peace officer or public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the computer data is in the person's possession or control when they receive the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.013(1) the justice or judge may order the person to preserve computer data` MEANS
    IF `the application is made ex parte by a peace officer or public officer` AND `the computer data is in the person's possession or control when they receive the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer, a justice or judge may order a person to preserve computer data that is in their possession or control when they receive the order"

-- src:9089 | Conditions for making order
-- src:9090 | (2) Before making the order, the justice or judge must be satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.002
-- src:9091 | (a) that there are reasonable grounds to suspect that an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament or has been committed under a law of a foreign state, that the computer data is in the person’s possession or control and that it will assist in the investigation of the offence; and
-- src:9092 | (b) that a peace officer or public officer intends to apply or has applied for a warrant or an order in connection with the investigation to obtain a document that contains the computer data.
@ref s 487.013(2) (src:9089-9092)
GIVEN `the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.002` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to suspect that an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament or has been committed under a law of a foreign state, that the computer data is in the person's possession or control and that it will assist in the investigation of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a peace officer or public officer intends to apply or has applied for a warrant or an order in connection with the investigation to obtain a document that contains the computer data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.013(2) the justice or judge has the satisfaction required before making the order` MEANS
    IF `the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.002`
       AND `there are reasonable grounds to suspect that an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament or has been committed under a law of a foreign state, that the computer data is in the person's possession or control and that it will assist in the investigation of the offence`
       AND `a peace officer or public officer intends to apply or has applied for a warrant or an order in connection with the investigation to obtain a document that contains the computer data`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.002"


-- 487.013(3) If an offence has been committed under a law of a foreign state, the justice or judge must also be satisfied that a person or authority with responsibility in that state for the investigation of such offences is conducting the investigation.
-- src:9093 | Offence against law of foreign state
-- src:9094 | (3) If an offence has been committed under a law of a foreign state, the justice or judge must also be satisfied that a person or authority with responsibility in that state for the investigation of such offences is conducting the investigation.
@ref s 487.013(3) (src:9093-9094)
GIVEN `the offence has been committed under a law of a foreign state` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice or judge is satisfied that a person or authority with responsibility in that state for the investigation of such offences is conducting the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.013(3) the justice or judge has the further satisfaction required for an offence against a law of a foreign state` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the offence has been committed under a law of a foreign state`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an offence has been committed under a law of a foreign state"
    ELSE IF `the justice or judge is satisfied that a person or authority with responsibility in that state for the investigation of such offences is conducting the investigation`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the justice or judge must also be satisfied that a person or authority with responsibility in that state for the investigation of such offences is conducting the investigation"

