-- src:9099 | Expiry of order
-- src:9100 | (6) Unless the order is revoked earlier, it expires 90 days after the day on which it is made.
@ref s 487.013(6) (src:9099-9100)
GIVEN `the day the order is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 487.013(6) the order expires on the day` MEANS `the day the order is made` PLUS 90

@ref s 487.013(6) (src:9099-9100)
GIVEN `the day the order is made` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the day the order was revoked, if it was revoked earlier` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.013(6) the order is in effect on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the order was revoked, if it was revoked earlier`
    WHEN JUST revoked THEN
        IF `the day in question` AT LEAST revoked
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless the order is revoked earlier"
        ELSE IF `the day in question` LESS THAN `s 487.013(6) the order expires on the day` `the day the order is made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it expires 90 days after the day on which it is made"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the day in question` LESS THAN `s 487.013(6) the order expires on the day` `the day the order is made`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it expires 90 days after the day on which it is made"


§ `Section 487.0131 -- Keep account open or active order`

-- 487.0131(1) On ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer, a justice or judge may order a person to keep an account specified in the order open or active unless the holder of the account requests that the person close or deactivate the account.
-- src:9101 | Keep account open or active order
-- src:9102 | 487.0131 (1) On ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer, a justice or judge may order a person to keep an account specified in the order open or active unless the holder of the account requests that the person close or deactivate the account.
@ref s 487.0131(1) (the power) (src:9101-9102)
GIVEN `the application is made ex parte by a peace officer or public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0131(1) the justice or judge may order the person to keep the account open or active` MEANS
    IF `the application is made ex parte by a peace officer or public officer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer, a justice or judge may order a person to keep an account specified in the order open or active"

-- src:9101 | Keep account open or active order
-- src:9102 | 487.0131 (1) On ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer, a justice or judge may order a person to keep an account specified in the order open or active unless the holder of the account requests that the person close or deactivate the account.
@ref s 487.0131(1) (the holder's request) (src:9101-9102)
GIVEN `an order is made to keep the account open or active` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder of the account requests that the person close or deactivate the account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0131(1) the person must keep the account open or active` MEANS
    IF (NOT `an order is made to keep the account open or active`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a justice or judge may order a person to keep an account specified in the order open or active"
    ELSE IF `the holder of the account requests that the person close or deactivate the account`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the holder of the account requests that the person close or deactivate the account"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:9103 | Conditions for making order
-- src:9104 | (2) Before making the order, the justice or judge must be satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.0031 that there are reasonable grounds to suspect that
-- src:9105 | (a) an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament; and
-- src:9106 | (b) keeping the account open or active will assist in the investigation of the offence.
@ref s 487.0131(2) (src:9103-9106)
GIVEN `the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.0031` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to suspect that an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds to suspect that keeping the account open or active will assist in the investigation of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0131(2) the justice or judge has the satisfaction required before making the order` MEANS
    IF `the justice or judge is satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.0031`
       AND `there are reasonable grounds to suspect that an offence has been or will be committed under this or any other Act of Parliament`
       AND `there are reasonable grounds to suspect that keeping the account open or active will assist in the investigation of the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be satisfied by information on oath in Form 5.0031"

-- src:9107 | Form
-- src:9108 | (3) The order is to be in Form 5.0032.
@ref s 487.0131(3) (src:9107-9108)
GIVEN `the order is in Form 5.0032` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0131(3) the order is in Form 5.0032` MEANS
    IF `the order is in Form 5.0032`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The order is to be in Form 5.0032"


-- 487.0131(4) The order is to require the person to notify a peace officer or public officer named in the order as soon as practicable after the account is closed or deactivated at the request of the holder of the account.
-- src:9109 | Notification
-- src:9110 | (4) The order is to require the person to notify a peace officer or public officer named in the order as soon as practicable after the account is closed or deactivated at the request of the holder of the account.
@ref s 487.0131(4) (src:9109-9110)
GIVEN `the order requires the person to notify a peace officer or public officer named in the order as soon as practicable after the account is closed or deactivated at the request of the holder of the account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0131(4) the order contains the notification requirement` MEANS
    IF `the order requires the person to notify a peace officer or public officer named in the order as soon as practicable after the account is closed or deactivated at the request of the holder of the account`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The order is to require the person to notify a peace officer or public officer named in the order"

-- src:9111 | Limitation
-- src:9112 | (5) A person who is under investigation for the offence referred to in subsection (2) may not be made subject to an order.
@ref s 487.0131(5) (src:9111-9112)
GIVEN `the person is under investigation for the offence referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0131(5) the order is barred against the person under investigation for the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person is under investigation for the offence referred to in subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is under investigation for the offence referred to in subsection (2) may not be made subject to an order"

-- src:9113 | Expiry of order
-- src:9114 | (6) Unless the order is revoked earlier, it expires 60 days after the day on which it is made.
@ref s 487.0131(6) (src:9113-9114)
GIVEN `the day the order is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 487.0131(6) the order expires on the day` MEANS `the day the order is made` PLUS 60

@ref s 487.0131(6) (src:9113-9114)
GIVEN `the day the order is made` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the day the order was revoked, if it was revoked earlier` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0131(6) the order is in effect on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day the order was revoked, if it was revoked earlier`
    WHEN JUST revoked THEN
        IF `the day in question` AT LEAST revoked
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Unless the order is revoked earlier"
        ELSE IF `the day in question` LESS THAN `s 487.0131(6) the order expires on the day` `the day the order is made` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it expires 60 days after the day on which it is made"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the day in question` LESS THAN `s 487.0131(6) the order expires on the day` `the day the order is made`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it expires 60 days after the day on which it is made"

-- src:9115 | Renewals
-- src:9116 | (7) A justice or judge may renew the order for a period of not more than 60 days on ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer indicating the reason and period for which the renewal is required.
@ref s 487.0131(7) (src:9115-9116)
GIVEN `the application is made ex parte by a peace officer or public officer indicating the reason and period for which the renewal is required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of the renewal, in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.0131(7) the justice or judge may renew the order for the period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the application is made ex parte by a peace officer or public officer indicating the reason and period for which the renewal is required`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on ex parte application made by a peace officer or public officer indicating the reason and period for which the renewal is required"
        IF (`the period of the renewal, in days` GREATER THAN 60) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a period of not more than 60 days"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

